A||||12||FieroLisa||Ohhh the goodness of Grand Am brakes!!!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||09-23-2001||06:13 PM||||I spent the weekend upgrading my brakes to the grand am conversion- wow what a difference!!!  New rotors, calipers, braided steel brake lines, hubs and master cylinder ran me just under $400 and a 10 hour exhausting day!!!!!!! I think I got dirtier doing that than I ever have before in my life. Chris Moore was the one helping me learn how to do this, and altho we had some probs with the hubs, it all went smoothly (and still took the entire day!) Except that he almost took my thumb off, but things like that happen, right??<P>But it was a good weekend and my car actually stops now!! (some of you may know my fluid was basically sludge and I blew a seal and well it wasn't a pretty site!!!)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-23-2001||06:38 PM||||I upgraded (if that's what you want to call it) all 4 corners on the Grape Ape, SS braided brake lines, Blazer MC, etc, etc.  I was very unimpressed.  What a waste of money, IMO.  Glad you like yours.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-23-2001||06:50 PM||||It must have been the weekend for brake jobs! I spent Saturday installing rebuilt calipers and new braided lines on the GT. The pads that were supplied to me are "Copper Top" brand. So far, the 88's new brakes are very impressive!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brian87egotrip||09-23-2001||07:08 PM||||I upgraded mine. I love it! Only took me 4 hours.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
